Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.870 align:start position:0%
 
when you first load up the game  in cyberpunk 2077 you'll be greeted by a  character creation screen  but before rushing through the section  you should know that your choices will  carry some significance into the main  story  and one of these decisions is around the  life path of your character  so which one should you choose  even a small cosmetic detail could have  some impact on the way that the story  plays out  and when it comes to choosing your life  path this is no different  it isn't just to give your character a  small backstory and set the mood  your life path will serve as the  guideline for defining your personal  story  who you know who knows you and also the  choices you can make in quests  each path has a different starting quest  and location  it will also determine how others will  react to you your dialogue choices  and even how some of your relationships  will play out  for example a nomad will be much better  at communicating and getting assistance  from other nomads and inhabitants of the  badlands  a street kid knows all the street level  drugs dealers  and fixes of night city and a corporate  is more savvy when dealing with mega  corporations and their agents  your road to main quests beginning  alliances and essentially the way you  will complete the story  is unique to each life path  with all the excitement around the  action and bright lights of night city  it's easy to forget about the enormous  desert that surrounds the city  and the people who live there referred  to as nomads  these outsiders to the big cities came  together during the collapse in the 90s  many people lost their jobs and were  forced from their homes  a large number of families left the  cities and started banding together  to create convoys that would travel from  place to place  salvaging attacking fuel depots and  raiding corporate facilities for weapons  and vehicles  members take on different roles like  doctors teachers  and farmers in order to ensure the  continuation from generation to  generation  these tribes or clans are essentially a  village  on wheels the vast desert around night  city is a dangerous place  ravaged by wars pollution and global  warming  the nomads also need to watch out for  any mega court mercenaries  that manage to cross their path as  corporations tend to not be a big fan of  this stuff being stolen  regardless of what they do to survive  nomads are often seen maintaining old  world values  they place importance on community and  maintain a more traditional society  where all people are equal and have the  same opportunities  work ethic and family are important to  them  naturally this means that the nomads are  not particularly fond of corporations  and gangs  and will go out of their way to defy any  structure that has been put in place by  them  they place much higher value towards  integrity and freedom  however in cyberpunk 2077 choosing the  nomad life path will have you starting  out on your own  something has happened to your family  forcing you to leave the badlands  and enter the completely unfamiliar  territory of night city  born and raised in night city street  kids are accustomed to the lawless  and unforgiving nature of the large city  they have learned to survive in a  hostile environment  where might makes right  after the economic collapse in america  street children make up the majority of  youth  due to a combination of lack of public  schooling system  and increased workloads results in a  lack of supervision  by the age of six most strict kids are  left unsupervised for up to six hours  a day by the age of 12 this figure  almost triples  to 16 hours a day almost 90  of street kids are involved in some type  of youth gang  which often have affiliations to larger  more aggressive street gangs  by the time they have reached  adolescence if they have been lucky  enough to survive this long  they are often inducted into the parent  gang that they have worked alongside in  their youth  street kids know the city like the back  of their hand those who were able to  survive this far  have done so through their connections  and street smarts  knowing the local slang drug dealers and  fixers  is all a part of life learning to  survive on the streets  and depending on certain people as if  they're a family  positions of authority like the police  or corporate security  are avoided at all costs without the  money to protect themselves  street kids are often abused by the  police and other groups with power  so to keep surviving it's best to stay  out of this site  choosing the street kid life path will  have you armed with intuitive knowledge  of the streets  relationships with smaller gangs and  aggressive fixes  will be far less hostile drug dealings  the black market and the social  hierarchy of night city  will be of comfortable familiarity on  your path  the street kit is the ultimate insider  of the goings-on in the underbelly of  night city  nicknamed corporates they are the  managers employees  and agents who work for mega  corporations  [Music]  although their life may seem  particularly comfortable in comparison  to the average person  it is certainly no less dangerous  in the hugely competitive corporate  world corporates will go out of their  way to sabotage their rivals  or even colleagues in order to increase  their chances of climbing through the  ranks  power struggles dirty tricks and  backstabbing  are all a part of the lifestyle  corporates are generally cold  calculating and relentless  arasaka is a worldwide maker corporation  dealing in corporate security  banking and manufacturing it is one of  the most influential maker corporations  in the world and it's here that you can  find some of the largest levels  of in-house fighting around corporates  who are willing to bend the rules  and exploit secrets and information are  the ones who are quickly climbing the  corporate ladder  know the most powerful and influential  people in the city  they are able to read between the lines  and remain completely calm in front of  even the most intimidating people  their knowledge and power leads to doors  being opened that would otherwise be  unattainable for the average person  choosing the corporate life path will  have you placed in the high pressured  position of an arasaka agent  you will be located in arasaka tower  where you will be expected to navigate  the eternal affairs within the  corporation  as well as seize opportunities by  spending negotiations  and contracts in your favor but what  would happen if arasaka  night city's most powerful organization  suddenly turns  on you  so which life path to choose of course  there is no right or wrong answer here  but i probably suggest taking the path  that sounds most like how you would like  to play the game  on the first run through you'll have a  more immersive experience  so choosing the role that would more  likely follow your way of thinking and  the decisions you make  will only support this for example i  think i'll be starting out with nomad  of course i want to experience all the  game has to offer but on the first run i  want to be able to take  everything in at the right pace the game  is centered around night city  so by starting in the badlands i feel  like it would be a nice build up as the  nomad makes his way to the big city  after all the nomad is completely  unfamiliar with night city  and would be experiencing it for the  first time like myself  but at the end of the day it really  doesn't matter that much you can always  start over with one of the other life  paths  or you could completely ignore the  stereotype of the role you pick  and play it like you want like maybe you  could try playing a corporate  as a kind friendly person to everyone  around you i'm sure that will work out  fine  anyway i hope this video has helped  clear up some of the differences between  the life paths  let me know in the comments which one  you think you'll be starting with  otherwise thank you very much for  watching  and i'll catch you in the next one  cheers  [Music]  you

